<title>POLAND: PBR TO PAY ADDITIONAL PLN 2.3 MLN TAX.</title>
<headline>PBR TO PAY ADDITIONAL PLN 2.3 MLN TAX.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A tax office in Warsaw has decided that Polish Development Bank (PBR) must pay 2.3 million zlotys in income tax for underpaid tax in 1994, PBR said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>PBR said it would appeal the decision with the supreme tax authorities in Warsaw.</p>
<p>PBR said the tax office demanded that the bank pay the additional tax after it found that PBR's 1994 costs and revenues were not properly registered in its tax statement for that year.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
